{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>You are still exalting yourself against My people.</b> As the Targum renders: כְּבִישַׁת בֵּהּ בְּעַמִּי. It is from the root מְסִלָּה — for we translate אֹרַח as כְּבִישָׁא, and in la'az קלקי״ר. And I have already explained at the end of וַיְהִי מִקֵּץ: any word whose root-letter foundation begins with samekh and it comes to speak in the reflexive (hitpa'el) binyan, the tav of the hitpa'el prefix is inserted into the middle of the root letters — as in this case, and as in ״וְיִסְתַּבֵּל הֶחָגָב״ (Ecclesiastes 12), from the root סבל; ״כִּי תִשְׂתָּרֵר עָלֵינוּ״ (Numbers 16), from the root נָגִיד and שָׂר; ״מִשְׂתַּכֵּל הֲוֵית״ (Daniel 7)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "the la'az קלקי״ר is Old French cauchier, 'to trample/tread'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:15.169496956Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}